  "units": [
    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " An iterator that maps the values of `iter` with `f`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            301,
            357
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            358,
            361
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This `struct` is created by the [`map`] method on [`Iterator`]. See its",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            362,
            437
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " documentation for more.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            438,
            465
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            466,
            469
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`map`]: Iterator::map",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            470,
            496
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`Iterator`]: trait.Iterator.html",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            497,
            534
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            535,
            538
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # Notes about side effects",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            539,
            569
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            570,
            573
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The [`map`] iterator implements [`DoubleEndedIterator`], meaning that",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            574,
            647
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " you can also [`map`] backwards:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            648,
            683
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            684,
            687
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```rust",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            688,
            699
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let v: Vec<i32> = [1, 2, 3].into_iter().map(|x| x + 1).rev().collect();",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            700,
            775
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            776,
            779
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " assert_eq!(v, [4, 3, 2]);",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            780,
            809
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            810,
            817
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            818,
            821
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`DoubleEndedIterator`]: trait.DoubleEndedIterator.html",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            822,
            881
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            882,
            885
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " But if your closure has state, iterating backwards may act in a way you do",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            886,
            964
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " not expect. Let's go through an example. First, in the forward direction:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            965,
            1042
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1043,
            1046
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```rust",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1047,
            1058
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let mut c = 0;",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1059,
            1077
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1078,
            1081
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " for pair in ['a', 'b', 'c'].into_iter()",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1082,
            1125
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "                                .map(|letter| { c += 1; (letter, c) }) {",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1126,
            1201
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     println!(\"{pair:?}\");",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1202,
            1231
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " }",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1232,
            1237
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1238,
            1245
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1246,
            1249
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This will print `('a', 1), ('b', 2), ('c', 3)`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1250,
            1301
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1302,
            1305
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Now consider this twist where we add a call to `rev`. This version will",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1306,
            1381
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " print `('c', 1), ('b', 2), ('a', 3)`. Note that the letters are reversed,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1382,
            1459
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " but the values of the counter still go in order. This is because `map()` is",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1460,
            1539
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " still being called lazily on each item, but we are popping items off the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1540,
            1616
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " back of the vector now, instead of shifting them from the front.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1617,
            1685
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1686,
            1689
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```rust",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1690,
            1701
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let mut c = 0;",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1702,
            1720
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1721,
            1724
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " for pair in ['a', 'b', 'c'].into_iter()",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1725,
            1768
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "                                .map(|letter| { c += 1; (letter, c) })",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1769,
            1842
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "                                .rev() {",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1843,
            1886
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     println!(\"{pair:?}\");",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1887,
            1916
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " }",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1917,
            1922
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1923,
            1930
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "must_use",
          "range": [
            1931,
